{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/78757-behind-the-curtain-and-normal-infrastructure","id":78757,"title":"Behind the Curtain and normal Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-24T16:18:02-08:00","id":78757,"title":"Behind the Curtain and normal Infrastructure","content":"So, do the teleportation tunnels described in this Exploit naturally exist in all infrastructure?<br /> <br /> How often do homeless people wander into infrastructure and wander out in like, Tokyo?<br /> <br /> ... how often are they caught?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:24:04-08:00","id":78765,"title":"","content":"I always thought of it as an inherent part of all Infrastructure, though I admit that I didn't take accidental usage into account. In my head Infrastructure acts as part of a mass transit network that all angels can use, as well as the refueling station and the beachhead into material reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T16:28:52-08:00","id":78775,"title":"","content":"A secondary concern:<br /> <br /> Can Suborned Infrastructure be accessed via the Exploit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T19:01:37-08:00","id":78942,"title":"","content":"Given that it requires an exploit to use, I don't see anyone accidentally wandering through any of those points. There may be more proper teleporters inside Facilities, but the Exploitation of more common Infrastructure sites involves the Demon messing with their own bodies in weird ways, like somehow achieving the effect by sticking their fingers in a power socket rather than stepping through a proper portal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T19:11:55-08:00","id":78962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/78757-behind-the-curtain-and-normal-infrastructure?p=78765#post78765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought of it as an inherent part of all Infrastructure, though I admit that I didn't take accidental usage into account. In my head Infrastructure acts as part of a mass transit network that all angels can use, as well as the refueling station and the beachhead into material reality.</div> </div> </div> </div> To use the God Machine = the Internet analogy I'm fond of... Angels (and demons with the right tricks) can transfer their &quot;information&quot; across the world wide Interface of the God Machine and go wherever they need to. <br /> <br /> Subborned Infrastructure, by definition, is cut off from the God Machine, and thus you're not hooked up to the GM &quot;Internet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyways, given how difficult it is for the average person to even SEE any of the GM's gears or Infrastructure, or even stumble onto it so they become stigmatic, I would have to say the chances of some random person getting sucked up is pretty low. Not zero, of course, but very low. Still would make an awesome plot hook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:35:51-08:00","id":80650,"title":"","content":"Sorry to join this late, but I seem to recall a City-Walker merit in the GM book. Pretty much covers normal people being able to transport from city to city like this, albeit on purpose by the mortal and with a supernatural power. Put a spin on it: the power only works between infrastructures or it's a feature of a particular set of infrastructures and you could conceivably have a clueless mortal that happens to see the gears in one piece of infrastructure, then walk out in a new city as a stigmatic with this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}